How to configure Nokia routers to receive and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes advertised by EBGP peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to receive and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes advertised by EBGP peers, you need to enable the `extended-nh-encoding` feature with the `ipv6` option. However, the provided reference content does not explicitly mention the `ipv6` option for `extended-nh-encoding`. Given the available options, you can configure the following commands:

```cli
config>router>bgp
  extended-nh-encoding ipv6
```

This command instructs BGP to advertise and recognize extended next-hop encoding capabilities for IPv6 routes, which may include the link-bandwidth extended community. Ensure that your EBGP peers also support this feature to properly advertise and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community.
