## User question:
Enable VPN IPv6 and label IPv4 routes to be advertised with an IPv6 next-hop address for BGP sessions over IPv6 transport on a Nokia router.
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable VPN IPv6 and label IPv4 routes to be advertised with an IPv6 next-hop address for BGP sessions over IPv6 transport on a Nokia router, you need to configure the following commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv6
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv6

config>router>bgp
    advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6
    advertise-ipv6-next-hops label-ipv6
    advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4
    advertise-ipv6-next-hops label-ipv4

config>router>bgp>group
    next-hop-self
```

These commands ensure that the necessary capabilities are advertised and that routes are advertised with the correct next-hop addresses over IPv6 transport.
