---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to allow advertising active /32 LDP FEC prefixes to a BGP peer with an RFC 3107 label, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix, you need to ensure that the router is capable of handling extended next-hop encoding for label IPv4 routes. Here are the necessary CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4

config>router>bgp>group <group-name>
    neighbor <peer-ip>
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group and `<peer-ip>` with the IP address of your BGP peer.
