## User question:
How to configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self, you need to follow these steps:

1. Enter the BGP configuration mode:
   ```
   config>router>bgp
   ```

2. Enable the link-bandwidth feature:
   ```
   link-bandwidth
   ```

3. Configure the BGP neighbor to use next-hop-self:
   ```
   neighbor <neighbor-ip> next-hop-self
   ```

4. Ensure that the BGP neighbor is configured to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities:
   ```
   neighbor <neighbor-ip> route-map <route-map-name> out
   route-map <route-map-name> permit 10
   set community <aggregate-community-value>
   ```

Replace `<neighbor-ip>` with the IP address of the BGP neighbor and `<route-map-name>` with the name of the route map that you create to aggregate the bandwidth values. Also, replace `<aggregate-community-value>` with the appropriate community value for aggregation.

Note: The reference content does not provide specific commands for aggregating bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities. The above configuration assumes that you have a route map in place to handle the aggregation logic. You would need to define the route map according to your specific requirements.
