undo segment-routing ipv6 best-effort
查询的def
The segment-routing ipv6 best-effort command enables a device to perform public network route iteration based on SIDs carried in routes.
The undo segment-routing ipv6 best-effort command disables a device from performing public network route iteration based on SIDs carried in routes.
By default, this function is disabled.
检索到的def
This command configures BGP to advertise (at session OPEN) the capability to receive label IPv4, VPN IPv4 routes, or IPv6 next hops from the peers. These peers should not send such routes unless they receive notification of this capability. If the SR OS router receives a label IPv4 or VPN IPv4 route from a peer to which it did not advertise the necessary capability, the UPDATE message will be considered malformed and this will cause either session reset ortreat-as-withdrawbehavior depending on the error handling settings.
检索到的def
This command configures the add-paths capability for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes. By default, add-paths is not enabled for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes.
