## User question:
"How to configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self, you need to follow these steps:

1. Enter the BGP configuration mode:
   ```
   config>router>bgp
   ```

2. Enable the link-bandwidth feature:
   ```
   link-bandwidth
   ```

3. Configure the BGP group to handle link-bandwidth extended communities:
   ```
   group <group-name>
   link-bandwidth
   ```

4. Configure the BGP neighbor to handle link-bandwidth extended communities:
   ```
   neighbor <neighbor-ip> link-bandwidth
   ```

5. Configure the BGP route aggregation to include link-bandwidth information:
   ```
   aggregate-address <network> <mask> attribute-policy <policy-name>
   ```

6. Define the policy to aggregate link-bandwidth information:
   ```
   policy>route-aggregation
   policy>route-aggregation>attribute-policy <policy-name>
   policy>route-aggregation>attribute-policy>set link-bandwidth <community-value>
   ```

7. Configure the BGP neighbor to use next-hop-self:
   ```
   neighbor <neighbor-ip> next-hop-self
   ```

Note: Replace `<group-name>`, `<neighbor-ip>`, `<network>`, `<mask>`, and `<policy-name>` with appropriate values for your network configuration.
