## User question:
How to enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes spanning multiple ASes on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes spanning multiple ASes on a Nokia router, you need to configure the `ignore-nh-metric` command under the `config>router>bgp>best-path-selection` context. This command instructs BGP to disregard the resolved distance to the BGP next-hop in its decision process for selecting the best route to a destination.

Here is the appropriate CLI configuration command:

```
config>router>bgp>best-path-selection
  ignore-nh-metric
```
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
aigp
no aigp
FuncDef:
This command enables or disables Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute support with one or more BGP peers. BGP path selection among routes with an associated AIGP metric is based on the end-to-end IGP metrics of the different BGP paths, even when these BGP paths span more than one AS and IGP instance.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
