## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router's BGP group to use route reflector cluster ID 192.168.10.5 with ORR location 8 and enable local fallback when no optimal routes are available?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the Nokia router's BGP group to use route reflector cluster ID 192.168.10.5 with ORR location 8 and enable local fallback when no optimal routes are available, you can use the following CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
config-router-bgp>group my-group-name
config-router-bgp-group>cluster 192.168.10.5 orr-location 8 allow-local-fallback
```

Replace `my-group-name` with the desired name for your BGP peer group.
