## User question:
How to configure Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default, you need to ensure that the BGP group is set up to recognize and handle EVPN routes appropriately. However, the provided reference content does not contain specific commands to directly handle EVPN routes or their encapsulation. Instead, we can focus on ensuring that the BGP group is properly configured to handle EVPN routes.

Here is the appropriate configuration:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
  config>router>bgp>group <group-name>
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
  end
end
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the actual name of your BGP group. This configuration ensures that the BGP group is capable of receiving and handling EVPN routes with VXLAN encapsulation.
---
