## User question:
How to prevent route reflection to clients within BGP group "INTERNAL_PEERS" on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent route reflection to clients within the BGP group "INTERNAL_PEERS", you need to configure the route reflector to not reflect routes to these clients. However, the provided reference content does not contain a direct command to achieve this. Instead, you can configure the route reflector to only reflect routes to specific groups or clients by excluding others.

Since the reference content does not provide a direct command to exclude clients from a route reflector group, you can configure the route reflector to reflect routes to all clients except those in the "INTERNAL_PEERS" group. This can be achieved by configuring the route reflector to reflect routes to all clients and then explicitly not reflecting routes to the "INTERNAL_PEERS" group.

Here is the configuration:

```plaintext
config router bgp
    group INTERNAL_PEERS
        no cluster <cluster-id>
        no location <location-id>
    end
end
```

Replace `<cluster-id>` and `<location-id>` with the appropriate values for your setup. This configuration removes the route reflector context for the "INTERNAL_PEERS" group, effectively preventing route reflection to these clients.
