## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to prevent BGP sessions from using fast external failover?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP sessions from using fast external failover, you can configure the `local-preference` command to set a lower preference for the fast external path. This will make the router prefer other paths over the fast external one. Here is an example of how to configure this:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    local-preference 100
```

This sets the local preference to 100, which is lower than the default value, thus discouraging the use of the fast external failover path. Adjust the value as necessary based on your network requirements.
