## User question:
"How to configure origin validation processing for both labeled IPv4 and unlabeled IPv6 routes on a Nokia router?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure origin validation processing for both labeled IPv4 and unlabeled IPv6 routes on a Nokia router, you need to use the `enable-origin-validation` command with the appropriate parameters. Here are the configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>group
    enable-origin-validation ipv6
    enable-origin-validation label-ipv4

config>router>bgp>group>neighbor
    enable-origin-validation ipv6
    enable-origin-validation label-ipv4
```

These commands enable origin validation processing for unlabeled IPv6 routes (`ipv6`) and labeled IPv4 routes (`label-ipv4`). Make sure to apply these configurations under the appropriate BGP group or neighbor contexts where you want to enforce origin validation.
