To configure a Nokia router to restrict BGP next-hop resolution to only use labeled routes from tunnels that have been explicitly marked with admin tags, you would need to use the `policy` command to define a route policy that enforces the use of labeled routes with admin tags. However, the provided reference content does not include a direct command to mark routes with admin tags or to enforce the use of such tagged routes specifically. 

Given the available commands, you can create a policy that allows only labeled routes and then apply this policy to the BGP next-hop resolution. Here is how you can do it:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>next-hop-resolution
