## User question:
"How to enable BGP extended community filtering in Nokia router CLI when configuring outbound route filtering?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP extended community filtering in the outbound route filtering configuration on a Nokia router, you need to configure the `outbound-route-filtering` command first. Then, you can apply extended community filters to the routes being advertised. Here are the CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
  outbound-route-filtering

config>router>bgp>group
  neighbor <neighbor-ip>
    extended-community-filter export <filter-name>

config>router>bgp>group
  neighbor <neighbor-ip>
    extended-community-filter import <filter-name>
```

Replace `<neighbor-ip>` with the IP address of the BGP neighbor and `<filter-name>` with the name of your extended community filter.
