How to configure next-hop-resolution options for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure next-hop-resolution options for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes on a Nokia router, you need to use the `policy` command under the `config>router>bgp>next-hop-resolution` context. Here is the appropriate CLI configuration command:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>next-hop-resolution
    policy <policy-name>
```

Replace `<policy-name>` with the name of your policy that controls which IPv6 routes are eligible to resolve the BGP next-hop addresses.
