undo network { <ipv4-address> [ <mask> | <mask-length> ] }
查询的def
The network command imports routes to the BGP routing table and advertises them to peers.
The undo network command cancels the configuration.
By default, BGP does not import routes.
检索到的def
This command enables the advertising of inactive BGP routes to other BGP peers. By default, BGP only advertises BGP routes to other BGP peers if a given BGP route is chosen by the route table manager as the most preferred route within the system and is active in the forwarding plane. This command allows system administrators to advertise a BGP route even though it is not the most preferred route within the system for a given destination.
检索到的def
This command configures BGP to advertise (at session OPEN) the capability to receive label IPv4, VPN IPv4 routes, or IPv6 next hops from the peers. These peers should not send such routes unless they receive notification of this capability. If the SR OS router receives a label IPv4 or VPN IPv4 route from a peer to which it did not advertise the necessary capability, the UPDATE message will be considered malformed and this will cause either session reset ortreat-as-withdrawbehavior depending on the error handling settings.
