## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to set the F bit to 1 for only non-forwarding AFI/SAFI families (L2-VPN, route-target, flow-IPv4, and flow-IPv6) during BGP graceful restart?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to set the F bit to 1 for only non-forwarding AFI/SAFI families (L2-VPN, route-target, flow-IPv4, and flow-IPv6) during BGP graceful restart, you would need to enable the `extended-nh-encoding` feature and specify the relevant AFI/SAFI families. However, the provided configuration manual does not include a direct command to set the F bit for specific AFI/SAFI families. Instead, you can enable the `extended-nh-encoding` for the required AFI/SAFI families as follows:

```cli
config>router>bgp>extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
config>router>bgp>extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
```

These commands instruct BGP to advertise the capability to receive label IPv4 and VPN IPv4 routes, which includes L2-VPN, route-target, flow-IPv4, and flow-IPv6 AFI/SAFI families. Note that the F bit is part of the BGP Graceful Restart mechanism and is typically managed through BGP capabilities negotiation, but the provided commands are the closest match to enabling the necessary features for BGP to handle these AFI/SAFI families.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
forwarding-bits-set { all | non-fwd }
no forwarding-bits-set
FuncDef:
This command determines the setting of the F bits in the GR and LLGR capabilities advertised by the router. When the F bit is set for an AFI/SAFI, it indicates that the advertising router was able to preserve forwarding state for the routes of that AFI/SAFI across the last restart. If a router restarts and does not set F=1, then when the session with a peer re-establishes the peer immediately deletes all LLGR stale routes it was preserving on behalf of the restarting router for the corresponding AFI/SAFI.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'all', 'Info': 'Specifies that the F bit for all AFI/SAFI should be set to 1.'}
{'Parameters': 'non-fwd', 'Info': 'Specifies that the F bit for only non-forwarding AFI/SAFI should be set to 1. These AFI/SAFI correspond to the following families: L2-VPN, route-target, flow-IPv4, and flow-IPv6.'}
