## User question:
"How to configure Nokia routers to impose a local LLGR stale time of 86400 seconds when receiving an LLGR capability from a BGP peer?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to impose a local LLGR stale time of 86400 seconds when receiving an LLGR capability from a BGP peer, you need to configure the `restart-time` command under the appropriate BGP view. Here is the CLI configuration command:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>graceful-restart>restart-time 86400
```

This command sets the restart-time to 86400 seconds, which will be advertised in the router's graceful-restart capability when receiving an LLGR capability from a BGP peer.
