How to configure BGP on a Nokia router to maintain the session permanently while rejecting any proposed hold-time below 120 seconds?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to maintain the session permanently while rejecting any proposed hold-time below 120 seconds, you need to set the `keepalive` timer to a value that ensures the session remains active and reject lower hold times by configuring the BGP neighbor with the desired hold time. Here are the appropriate CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    keepalive 30
    neighbor <peer-ip> timers 30 120
```

Replace `<peer-ip>` with the IP address of the BGP peer you want to configure. The `keepalive 30` command sets the keepalive timer to 30 seconds, and the `neighbor <peer-ip> timers 30 120` command sets the hold time to 120 seconds, ensuring that sessions with lower hold times are rejected.
