## User question:
"How to configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 alternate paths per unlabeled IPv4 prefix while disabling the ability to receive multiple paths from BGP peers?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 alternate paths per unlabeled IPv4 prefix while disabling the ability to receive multiple paths from BGP peers, you need to configure the `label-ipv4` command under the BGP configuration. Here are the appropriate CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    label-ipv4 send 8 receive none
```

This configuration sets the maximum number of paths per labeled-unicast IPv4 prefix to 8 and disables the negotiation to receive multiple labeled-unicast routes per IPv4 prefix.
