## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv4 paths per prefix and disable receiving multiple paths?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv4 paths per prefix and disable receiving multiple paths, you need to use the following CLI commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>label-ipv4 send 8
config>router>bgp>label-ipv4 receive none
```

These commands ensure that the router advertises up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv4 paths per prefix and does not negotiate or receive multiple paths.
