## User question:
How to enter the configuration context for setting up labeled route parameters in BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enter the configuration context for setting up labeled route parameters in BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, you need to configure the `policy` command under the `router bgp next-hop-resolution` context. Here is the appropriate CLI configuration command:

```
config>router>bgp>next-hop-resolution
policy <policy-name>
```

Replace `<policy-name>` with the desired name for your policy. This command sets up the policy that controls which IP routes in RTM are eligible to resolve the BGP next-hop addresses for IPv4 and IPv6 routes.
