## User question:
How to configure Nokia router to use LDP tunneling for resolving next-hops of /32 IPv4 FECs and /128 IPv6 FECs?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia router to use LDP tunneling for resolving next-hops of /32 IPv4 FECs and /128 IPv6 FECs, you need to enable the `extended-nh-encoding` feature with the appropriate parameters. Here are the configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
  extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
  extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
```

Additionally, ensure that the `allow-static` command is configured to allow static routes to resolve the next-hops for labeled routes:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>next-hop-res>labeled-routes
  allow-static
```

These commands will enable the router to use LDP tunneling for resolving next-hops of /32 IPv4 FECs and /128 IPv6 FECs.
