## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to attach a link-bandwidth extended community to BGP routes advertised from a specific neighbor?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to attach a link-bandwidth extended community to BGP routes advertised from a specific neighbor, you need to follow these steps:

1. Enter the BGP configuration mode.
2. Define the BGP group or neighbor where you want to apply the link-bandwidth extended community.
3. Configure the `send-to-ebgp` command to allow sending the link-bandwidth extended community to the specified neighbor.
4. Configure the `accept-from-ebgp` command to ensure that the router accepts and uses the link-bandwidth extended community from the specified neighbor.

Here are the corresponding CLI commands:

```plaintext
config> router> bgp> group> <group-name>
send-to-ebgp ipv4

config> router> bgp> group> <group-name> > neighbor> <neighbor-ip>
accept-from-ebgp ipv4
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group and `<neighbor-ip>` with the IP address of the specific neighbor from which you want to attach the link-bandwidth extended community.
