## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to discard routes received from a peer when detecting the local AS number 65530 in the AS path while maintaining the BGP session?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to discard routes received from a peer when detecting the local AS number 65530 in the AS path while maintaining the BGP session, you need to use the `enforce-first-as` command. Here are the CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config> router> bgp
config-router-bgp> group <group-name> ebgp
config-router-bgp-group> neighbor <neighbor-ip>
config-router-bgp-group-neighbor> enforce-first-as
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group and `<neighbor-ip>` with the IP address of the BGP peer. This configuration will ensure that routes received from the specified BGP peer are discarded if the most recent AS in the AS_PATH is 65530, while keeping the BGP session up.
---
