no loop-detect
FuncDef:
This command configures how the BGP peer session handles loop detection in the AS path.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'drop-peer', 'Info': 'Sends a notification to the remote peer and drops the session.'}
{'Parameters': 'discard-route', 'Info': 'Discards routes received from a peer with the same AS number as the router itself. This option prevents routes looped back to the router from being added to the routing information base and consuming memory. When this option is changed, the change will not be active for an established peer until the connection is re-established for the peer.'}
{'Parameters': 'ignore-loop', 'Info': 'Ignores routes with loops in the AS path but maintains peering.'}
{'Parameters': 'off', 'Info': 'Disables loop detection.'}
