## User question:
"How to configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with MED value set to 5000 when MED is not already specified?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with a MED value set to 5000 when MED is not already specified, you need to use the `always-compare-med` command with the `zero` parameter. Here are the necessary CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>best-path-selection
always-compare-med zero
```

After setting this configuration, any route that does not specify a MED value will be treated as having a MED value of 0, and you can then set the MED value to 5000 for specific routes using other BGP configuration commands.
