## User question:
Configure the TTL value for BGP packets to reach an EBGP peer located three hops away on a Nokia router.
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the TTL value for BGP packets to reach an EBGP peer located three hops away on a Nokia router, you need to set the minimum TTL value for the BGP neighbor. Since the peer is three hops away, you can set the `min-ttl-value` to 3.

Here are the configuration commands:

```
config>router>bgp>group>neighbor
set ttl-security 3
```
