## User question:
Enable BGP multipath on a Nokia router with maximum 8 paths for any prefix, allowing up to 12 paths for EBGP routes and restricting non-best paths to those sharing the exact AS path as the best path.
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP multipath on your Nokia router with the specified conditions, you need to configure the following commands:

```cli
router bgp <your-as-number>
  best-path selection multipath-relax
  maximum-paths 8
  maximum-paths ibgp 12
  enforce-first-as
```

Replace `<your-as-number>` with the actual AS number of your BGP router. This configuration will allow up to 8 paths for any prefix and up to 12 paths for EBGP routes, while ensuring that only non-best paths share the exact AS path as the best path.
