## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 3 paths per multicast VPN IPv6 prefix while disabling the ability to receive multiple paths for the same prefix?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 3 paths per multicast VPN IPv6 prefix while disabling the ability to receive multiple paths for the same prefix, you need to configure the `send` and `receive` parameters for the `vpn-ipv6` family under the `add-paths` command. Here are the appropriate CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>add-paths>vpn-ipv6 send 3 receive none
```

This command sets the maximum number of paths per prefix to 3 for sending and disables receiving multiple paths for the same prefix.
---
