## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to enable unchanged BGP next-hops for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in a specific group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to enable unchanged BGP next-hops for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in a specific group, you need to use the `next-hop-self` command under the BGP group or neighbor configuration. Here are the CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config> router> bgp
config-router-bgp> group <GROUP_NAME>
config-router-bgp-group> neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IP>
config-router-bgp-group-neighbor> next-hop-self
```

Replace `<GROUP_NAME>` with the name of your BGP group and `<NEIGHBOR_IP>` with the IP address of the peer you want to configure.

For IPv6, ensure that the same configuration is applied to the IPv6 neighbors:

```plaintext
config> router> bgp
config-router-bgp> group <GROUP_NAME>
config-router-bgp-group> neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IP_V6>
config-router-bgp-group-neighbor> next-hop-self
```

Replace `<NEIGHBOR_IP_V6>` with the IPv6 address of the peer you want to configure.
