## User question:
How to configure BGP on a Nokia router to enable optimal path selection for reflected routes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to enable optimal path selection for reflected routes, you need to ensure that the `next-hop-self` command is configured. Here are the appropriate CLI configuration commands:

```
config>router>bgp>group
  next-hop-self
```

If you have a specific neighbor or group where you want to apply this setting, you can do so as follows:

```
config>router>bgp>group<name>
  neighbor<ip-address>
    next-hop-self
```

Replace `<name>` with the name of your BGP group and `<ip-address>` with the IP address of the neighbor you want to configure.
