## User question:
How to disable BGP session initiation attempts while maintaining existing connections in a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To disable BGP session initiation attempts while maintaining existing connections in a Nokia router, you need to disable capability negotiation for the BGP group. Here is the appropriate CLI configuration command:

```
no router bgp group <group-name> disable-capability-negotiation
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name or identifier of your BGP group. This command will prevent the router from negotiating new capabilities with the specified BGP peer, effectively disabling BGP session initiation attempts for new sessions while keeping existing sessions intact.
