## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to generate a warning message when receiving 5000 IPv6 routes from a BGP peer, with a threshold alert at 80% capacity, without terminating the session?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to generate a warning message when receiving 5000 IPv6 routes from a BGP peer, with a threshold alert at 80% capacity, without terminating the session, you can use the following CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
prefix-limit ipv6 5000 threshold 80 log-only
```

This command sets the limit to 5000 IPv6 routes and configures a warning message to be sent when the threshold of 80% is reached, but it does not terminate the session.
