```

This command enables the context to configure options for the next-hop resolution of BGP labeled routes using tunnels in TTM. However, the reference content does not provide specific commands to set the address family for transport tunnels. Therefore, you would typically configure the address family through other means, such as setting the `policy` command to control the next-hop resolution process.

For example, you might use the `policy` command to specify a route policy that controls which IP routes in RTM are eligible to resolve the BGP next-hop addresses for the specific address family required by your transport tunnels.

Here is an example of how you might configure a policy:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>next-hop-resolution>policy <policy-name>
```

Replace `<policy-name>` with a suitable name for your policy. Then, define the policy rules to match the specific address family required by your transport tunnels.

If you need further customization or specific commands for the address family, please provide additional details or refer to the Nokia router documentation for more advanced configurations.
