## User question:
Configure Nokia routers to allow only BGP and SR-TE tunnel types for resolving unlabeled BGP routes.
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to allow only BGP and SR-TE tunnel types for resolving unlabeled BGP routes, you need to ensure that only these protocols are used for recursive resolution. However, the provided reference content does not contain a direct command to restrict the types of routes used for recursive resolution. Instead, we can focus on enabling the necessary protocols and disabling others.

Here are the relevant configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    use-bgp-routes

config>router>bgp>next-hop-res
    use-bgp-routes

config>router>bgp>group
    graceful-restart

config>router>bgp>group>neighbor
    graceful-restart

config>router>bgp>add-paths
    label-ipv6 send 16 receive none

config>router>bgp>extended-nh-encoding
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4

config>router>bgp>link-state-import-enable
```

These commands enable BGP for recursive route resolution, graceful restart, label-IPv6 add-paths, extended next-hop encoding for label-IPv4 and VPN-IPv4, and import of link-state information into the BGP-LS address family. Note that the `use-bgp-routes` command is used twice to ensure it applies at both the global BGP level and the next-hop resolution level.
