## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to enable BGP Monitoring Protocol (BMP) for sending only post-policy route monitoring messages?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to enable BGP Monitoring Protocol (BMP) for sending only post-policy route monitoring messages, you need to follow these steps:

1. Enter the configuration mode:
```
configure
```

2. Enable BMP globally:
```
bmp
```

3. Configure the BMP station and enable local route reporting:
```
bmp station
report-local-routes
```

4. Exit the station configuration mode:
```
exit
```

By enabling `report-local-routes`, the router will send post-policy route monitoring messages to the BMP monitoring station. If you want to disable sending pre-policy route monitoring messages, you can use the `no report-local-routes` command instead of the `report-local-routes` command.
