## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to enable BGP resolution of labeled-unicast route next-hops using the IGP route table when acting as a Route Reflector without tunnel signaling protocol participation?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to enable BGP resolution of labeled-unicast route next-hops using the IGP route table when acting as a Route Reflector without tunnel signaling protocol participation, you need to ensure that BGP is configured to handle extended next-hop encoding. Here are the necessary CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
    no disable-capability-negotiation
    router-id <your-router-id>
    no link-state-import-enable
    enable-notification
```

Replace `<your-router-id>` with the appropriate IP address for your router ID. This configuration ensures that BGP advertises the capability to receive label IPv4 routes, does not disable capability negotiation, sets a router ID, and enables BGP to use the IGP route table for labeled-unicast route next-hops while acting as a Route Reflector.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
