## User question:
Enable OSPF-based Segment Routing tunnel selection for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router.
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable OSPF-based Segment Routing tunnel selection for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, you need to configure the `extended-nh-encoding` feature to support label IPv4 next hops. Here are the necessary CLI configuration commands:

```shell
config>router>bgp>extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
```

This command instructs BGP to advertise an extended NH encoding capability for label IPv4 next hops, which is required for OSPF-based Segment Routing tunnel selection in BGP next-hop resolution.
