## User question:
How to enable BGP on a Nokia router to advertise locally configured segment routing policies as originated routes to peers supporting SR policy IPv4 address family?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP on a Nokia router to advertise locally configured segment routing policies as originated routes to peers supporting SR policy IPv4 address family, you need to configure the following commands:

1. Set the router ID:
```shell
router-id <your-router-id>
```
Replace `<your-router-id>` with the actual IP address you want to use as the router ID.

2. Enable BGP and specify the address family for SR policies:
```shell
config>router>bgp
router>bgp>group>neighbor>ipv4-unicast
```

3. Configure BGP to send link-bandwidth extended community to EBGP peers for IPv4 address family:
```shell
router>bgp>group>neighbor>link-bandwidth>send-to-ebgp ipv4
```

4. Configure BGP to accept link-bandwidth extended community from EBGP peers for IPv4 address family:
```shell
router>bgp>group>neighbor>link-bandwidth>accept-from-ebgp ipv4
```

5. Enable BGP to import link-state information into the BGP-LS address family:
```shell
config>router>bgp
link-state-import-enable
```

These commands should help you configure BGP on your Nokia router to meet the requirements specified in the user request. Make sure to replace placeholders with actual values specific to your network configuration.
