## User question:
How to enable BGP on a Nokia router to advertise locally configured segment routing policies as originated routes to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP on a Nokia router to advertise locally configured segment routing policies as originated routes to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family, you need to configure the following commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp
    router-id <your-router-id>
    graceful-restart
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
    label-ipv6 send 1 receive none
    router>address-family ipv4 unicast
        network <your-network>
        redistribute segment-routing-policy
    router>address-family ipv4 unicast
        exit
```

Replace `<your-router-id>` with the desired router ID and `<your-network>` with the network you want to redistribute. This configuration enables BGP, sets up the necessary capabilities, and redistributes the segment routing policies as IPv4 unicast routes.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
sr-policy-import
no sr-policy-import
FuncDef:
This command instructs BGP to import all statically-configured non-local segment routing policies from the segment routing DB into the BGP RIB so that they can be advertised, as originated routes, towards BGP peers supporting thesr-policy-ipv4address family.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
