## Proposed answer:
To enable TCP connection keepalive monitoring on a Nokia router's BMP station, you need to configure the `keep-interval` command under the `bmp station connection tcp-keepalive` context. Here are the configuration commands:

```
config
bmp
station
connection
tcp-keepalive
keep-interval <interval>
``` 

Replace `<interval>` with the desired value in seconds between 1 and 100000. For example, to set the interval to 30 seconds, you would use:

```
config
bmp
station
connection
tcp-keepalive
keep-interval 30
```
