## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop when advertising routes between EBGP peers within the same subnet?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop when advertising routes between EBGP peers within the same subnet, you need to use the `third-party-nexthop` command. Here are the appropriate CLI configuration commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>group>neighbor
third-party-nexthop
```

This command ensures that when an IPv4 or IPv6 route is received from one EBGP peer and advertised to another EBGP peer in the same IP subnet, the BGP next-hop is left unchanged.
