## User question:
How can BGP export route policies for VPN routes (including vpn-ipv4/6, mvpn-ipv4/6, l2-vpn, etc.) be enabled on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP export route policies for VPN routes including `vpn-ipv4`, `mvpn-ipv4`, `l2-vpn`, etc., on a Nokia router, you need to configure the following commands:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>add-paths
    mvpn-ipv4 send <send-limit> receive [ none ]
    mcast-vpn-ipv4 send <send-limit> receive [ none ]
    leak-import <plcy-or-long-expr> [ <plcy-or-expr> ]
```

Replace `<send-limit>` with the desired limit for the number of paths per prefix that are allowed to be advertised to add-paths peers. If you do not want to negotiate the send capability, you can set `send-limit` to `none`. For the `leak-import` command, replace `<plcy-or-long-expr>` and `<plcy-or-expr>` with your specific route policies.

Additionally, you might want to consider enabling the `ebgp-ibgp-equal` command to ensure that EBGP and IBGP routes are treated equally in the best path selection process:

```plaintext
config>router>bgp>best-path-selection
    ebgp-ibgp-equal [ ipv4 ] [ ipv6 ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ] [ vpn-ipv4 ] [ vpn-ipv6 ]
```

Replace `[ ipv4 ]`, `[ ipv6 ]`, `[ label-ipv4 ]`, `[ label-ipv6 ]`, `[ vpn-ipv4 ]`, and `[ vpn-ipv6 ]` with the relevant parameters based on your requirements.
